@* A toast with something to do. Keep it to an undo or a link: a toast disappears, so anything
   that has to be done cannot live only in one.

   `action: { label, onClick }` is sonner's shape, and the call site reads the same as it would
   there — which is the point of this whole file. Taking the action dismisses the toast, because
   a toast whose action has been taken has nothing left to say. *@
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <Button Variant="outline" Type="button"
            data-toast='{"text":"Order archived","type":"success","action":{"label":"Undo","toast":{"text":"Order restored"}}}'>
        With an undo
    </Button>
    <Button Variant="outline" Type="button"
            data-toast='{"text":"Payment failed","type":"error","action":{"label":"Retry","toast":{"text":"Payment taken","type":"success"}}}'>
        With a retry
    </Button>
</div>
